WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.400
Two more components.

2
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:05.630
Amazon Connect agents work in a
browser, and AWS says that traffic

3
00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:09.625
traverses the public network
and prefers a domain allowlist.

4
00:00:09.625 --> 00:00:12.671
If agents can't resolve
the media relay names,

5
00:00:12.671 --> 00:00:17.775
the softphone can't set up its media
channel, so don't over-restrict their DNS.

6
00:00:17.775 --> 00:00:21.929
In GovCloud, Connect is available
only in the US-West region,

7
00:00:21.929 --> 00:00:25.150
uses its own names, and
lacks several features.

8
00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:29.644
Private API access covers only
a subset of Connect, and,

9
00:00:29.644 --> 00:00:34.437
as an inference, helps API calls,
not the agent or voice path.

10
00:00:34.437 --> 00:00:38.528
On VMware, a Broadcom article
says changing vCenter's name

11
00:00:38.528 --> 00:00:42.363
or address is blocked if the
name doesn't fully resolve.

12
00:00:42.363 --> 00:00:44.487
So keep those records right in the Grid.

13
00:00:44.487 --> 00:00:46.250
Next, the subtle one.
